 6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

 You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
 of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
 machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
 in one of these ways:

   a) Convey the object code in, or embedded in, a physical product
      (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
      Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium
      (including a physical distribution medium) with the object code.

   b) Convey the object code in, or embedded in, a physical product
      (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
      written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
      long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that
      product, to give anyone who possesses the object code a copy of
      the Corresponding Source for all the software covered by this
      License on a durable physical medium at no more than your
      reasonable cost of performing this service, or, if you have the
      capability, to give the object code's recipient a copy of the
      Corresponding Source on a network server at no charge.

   c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
      Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
      physical distribution medium), at no charge to the recipient.

   d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
      place (gratis or at a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
      Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at
      no further charge. You need not supervise or coordinate the
      distribution of copies being made through this place. If you
      convey the object code through a network server, the
      Corresponding Source may be on a server operated by you or by
      a third party, with the Corresponding Source being accessible
      from the network server at no charge to anyone who possesses
      the object code, for the duration of the object code's
      availability to anyone from that network server.

   e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission,
      provided you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source
      and the object code are available to the general public at no
      charge. You must know the location of the Corresponding Source
      that the peer-to-peer network is using to provide access.

 A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is excluded
 from the Corresponding Source as a System Interface, need not be
 included in the Corresponding Source for the whole object code.

