 In the following three paragraphs, "party" means any party, and
 "you" means the licensee as a party to a particular transaction.

 If you convey a covered work, knowingly relying on a patent license,
 and you do not convey the Corresponding Source under this License,
 the party to which you convey the work may sue you for patent
 infringement. If such a suit results in a judgment that you are not
 liable, then the patent license that you relied on is invalid, and
 you may not use it. If the suit results in a judgment that you are
 liable, the patent license that you relied on is void, with respect
 to the claims at issue, and the party to which you conveyed the work
