 If, pursuant to or in connection with a single transaction, you
 convey, or any party conveys, a covered work, and you have a patent
 license from a third party that permits you to make, use, sell, offer
 for sale, or import the covered work, you must provide the
 Corresponding Source to the party to which the work is conveyed. If
 you do not provide the Corresponding Source, the party to which the
 work is conveyed may require you to do so under this License.

 If you do not provide the Corresponding Source as required by this
 License, then the party to which the work is conveyed may bring a
 patent infringement suit against you. If the judgment in that suit
 results in a license that is invalid or void, the patent license
 that you relied on is invalid or void, with respect to the claims at
 issue. This paragraph does not apply to the patent claims of a
 contributor that are not essential claims of that contributor.

